IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-logic`

-- ccc13-contract-intimidation.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part X: sections 422 to 427 (criminal breach of contract, intimidation, discrimination against
-- trade unionists, threats and retaliation against employees, secret commissions). Reading of the answers as in ccc13-fraud.l4.
-- "No person shall" and "No employer ... shall" are prohibitions: JUST TRUE when every element is met, NOTHING otherwise; each also has a SHANT rule.

§ `Part X -- sections 422 to 427`

§§ `Breach of Contract, Intimidation and Discrimination Against Trade Unionists -- sections 422 to 425.1`

-- (2) No person wilfully breaks a contract within the meaning of subsection (1) by reason only that (a) being the employee of an employer, he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and himself to agree on any matter relating to his employment, or,
-- (b) being a member of an organization of employees formed for the purpose of regulating relations between employers and employees, he stops work as a result of the failure of the employer and a bargaining agent acting on behalf of the organization to agree on any matter relating to the employment of members of the organization,
-- if, before the stoppage of work occurs, all steps provided by law with respect to the settlement of industrial disputes are taken and any provision for the final settlement of differences, without stoppage of work, contained in or by law deemed to be contained in a collective agreement is complied with and effect given thereto.
-- src:7515 | Saving
-- src:7516 | (2) No person wilfully breaks a contract within the meaning of subsection (1) by reason only that
-- src:7517 | (a) being the employee of an employer, he stops work as a result of the failure of his employer and himself to agree on any matter relating to his employment, or,
-- src:7518 | (b) being a member of an organization of employees formed for the purpose of regulating relations between employers and employees, he stops work as a result of the failure of the employer and a bargaining agent acting on behalf of the organization to agree on any matter relating to the employment of members of the organization,
-- src:7519 | if, before the stoppage of work occurs, all steps provided by law with respect to the settlement of industrial disputes are taken and any provision for the final settlement of differences, without stoppage of work, contained in or by law deemed to be contained in a collective agreement is complied with and effect given thereto.
@ref s 422(2) (src:7515-7519)
DECLARE `s 422(2) reason for stopping work` IS ONE OF
    `s 422(2) being the employee of an employer, the person stops work as a result of the failure of the employer and the person to agree on any matter relating to the person’s employment`   -- (a)
    `s 422(2) being a member of an organization of employees formed for the purpose of regulating relations between employers and employees, the person stops work as a result of the failure of the employer and a bargaining agent acting on behalf of the organization to agree on any matter relating to the employment of members of the organization`   -- (b)
    `s 422(2) a reason that is neither`

@ref s 422(2) (src:7515-7519)
GIVEN reason IS A `s 422(2) reason for stopping work`
      `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to have wilfully broken the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before the stoppage of work occurs, all steps provided by law with respect to the settlement of industrial disputes are taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any provision for the final settlement of differences, without stoppage of work, contained in or by law deemed to be contained in a collective agreement is complied with and effect given thereto` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 422(2) the person is saved from having wilfully broken a contract within the meaning of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF reason EQUALS `s 422(2) a reason that is neither`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving is stated for paragraphs (a) and (b); a stoppage for another reason is outside it
    ELSE IF `the stoppage is the only reason the person is said to have wilfully broken the contract` AND `before the stoppage of work occurs, all steps provided by law with respect to the settlement of industrial disputes are taken` AND `any provision for the final settlement of differences, without stoppage of work, contained in or by law deemed to be contained in a collective agreement is complied with and effect given thereto`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, before the stoppage of work occurs, all steps provided by law with respect to the settlement of industrial disputes are taken"; this subsection gives no saving on these facts

DECLARE `s 422(1) probable consequence` IS ONE OF
    `s 422(1) to endanger human life`   -- (a)
    `s 422(1) to cause serious bodily injury`   -- (b)
    `s 422(1) to expose valuable property, real or personal, to destruction or serious injury`   -- (c)
    `s 422(1) to deprive the inhabitants of a city or place, or part thereof, wholly or to a great extent, of their supply of light, power, gas or water`   -- (d)
    `s 422(1) to delay or prevent the running of any locomotive engine, tender, freight or passenger train or car, on a railway that is a common carrier`   -- (e)
    `s 422(1) a probable consequence that is none of those`

-- src:7504 | Breach of Contract, Intimidation and Discrimination Against Trade Unionists
-- src:7505 | Criminal breach of contract
-- src:7506 | 422 (1) Every one who wilfully breaks a contract, knowing or having reasonable cause to believe that the probable consequences of doing so, whether alone or in combination with others, will be
-- src:7507 | (a) to endanger human life,
-- src:7508 | (b) to cause serious bodily injury,
-- src:7509 | (c) to expose valuable property, real or personal, to destruction or serious injury,
-- src:7510 | (d) to deprive the inhabitants of a city or place, or part thereof, wholly or to a great extent, of their supply of light, power, gas or water, or
-- src:7511 | (e) to delay or prevent the running of any locomotive engine, tender, freight or passenger train or car, on a railway that is a common carrier,
-- src:7512 | is guilty of
-- src:7513 | (f) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years, or
-- src:7514 | (g) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 422(1) (src:7504-7514)
GIVEN `the person wilfully breaks a contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the probable consequences of doing so, whether alone or in combination with others, will be the consequence` IS A BOOLEAN
      consequence IS A `s 422(1) probable consequence`
      `the saving applies, by s 422(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` MEANS
    IF    `the person wilfully breaks a contract`
      AND `the person knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the probable consequences of doing so, whether alone or in combination with others, will be the consequence`
      AND NOT (consequence EQUALS `s 422(1) a probable consequence that is none of those`)
    THEN `ccc13 not` `the saving applies, by s 422(2)`   -- JUST FALSE when the saving applies; NOTHING carried
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who wilfully breaks a contract, knowing or having reasonable cause to believe that the probable consequences of doing so"

@ref s 422(1) (the punishments) (src:7504-7514)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 422(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 422(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7504-7514)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 422(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (3) No proceedings shall be instituted under this section without the consent of the Attorney General.
-- src:7520 | Consent required
-- src:7521 | (3) No proceedings shall be instituted under this section without the consent of the Attorney General.
@ref s 422(3) (src:7520-7521)
GIVEN `the consent of the Attorney General has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 422(3) the section bars the proceedings for want of the consent of the Attorney General` MEANS
    IF `the consent of the Attorney General has been given`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the Attorney General"; the subsection says nothing about proceedings that have the consent
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) A person who attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place, for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information, does not watch or beset within the meaning of this section.
-- src:7531 | Exception
-- src:7532 | (2) A person who attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place, for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information, does not watch or beset within the meaning of this section.
@ref s 423(2) (src:7531-7532)
GIVEN `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423(2) the person does not watch or beset within the meaning of section 423` MEANS
    IF `the person attends at or near or approaches a dwelling-house or place` AND `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information"; this subsection gives no saving on these facts

DECLARE `s 423(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 423(1) uses violence or threats of violence to that person or their intimate partner or children, or injures the person’s property`   -- (a)
    `s 423(1) intimidates or attempts to intimidate that person or a relative of that person by threats that, in Canada or elsewhere, violence or other injury will be done to or punishment inflicted on them or a relative of theirs, or that the property of any of them will be damaged`   -- (b)
    `s 423(1) persistently follows that person`   -- (c)
    `s 423(1) hides any tools, clothes or other property owned or used by that person, or deprives them of them or hinders them in the use of them`   -- (d)
    `s 423(1) with one or more other persons, follows that person, in a disorderly manner, on a highway`   -- (e)
    `s 423(1) besets or watches the place where that person resides, works, carries on business or happens to be`   -- (f)
    `s 423(1) blocks or obstructs a highway`   -- (g)
    `s 423(1) an act that is none of those`

-- 423 (1) Every one is guilty of ... who, wrongfully and without lawful authority, for the purpose of compelling another person to abstain from doing anything that he or she has a lawful right to do, or to do anything that he or she has a lawful right to abstain from doing, (a) ... (g).
-- src:7522 | Intimidation
-- src:7523 | 423 (1) Every one is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, wrongfully and without lawful authority, for the purpose of compelling another person to abstain from doing anything that he or she has a lawful right to do, or to do anything that he or she has a lawful right to abstain from doing,
-- src:7524 | (a) uses violence or threats of violence to that person or their intimate partner or children, or injures the person’s property;
-- src:7525 | (b) intimidates or attempts to intimidate that person or a relative of that person by threats that, in Canada or elsewhere, violence or other injury will be done to or punishment inflicted on him or her or a relative of his or hers, or that the property of any of them will be damaged;
-- src:7526 | (c) persistently follows that person;
-- src:7527 | (d) hides any tools, clothes or other property owned or used by that person, or deprives him or her of them or hinders him or her in the use of them;
-- src:7528 | (e) with one or more other persons, follows that person, in a disorderly manner, on a highway;
-- src:7529 | (f) besets or watches the place where that person resides, works, carries on business or happens to be; or
-- src:7530 | (g) blocks or obstructs a highway.
@ref s 423(1) (src:7522-7530)
GIVEN `the person acts wrongfully and without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to compel another person to abstain from doing anything that they have a lawful right to do, or to do anything that they have a lawful right to abstain from doing` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS A `s 423(1) act`
      `the saving applies, by s 423(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` MEANS
    IF    `the person acts wrongfully and without lawful authority`
      AND `the purpose is to compel another person to abstain from doing anything that they have a lawful right to do, or to do anything that they have a lawful right to abstain from doing`
      AND NOT (act EQUALS `s 423(1) an act that is none of those`)
    THEN IF act EQUALS `s 423(1) besets or watches the place where that person resides, works, carries on business or happens to be`
         THEN `ccc13 not` `the saving applies, by s 423(2)`   -- (f): subsection (2) says what does not watch or beset; JUST FALSE when it applies, NOTHING carried
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, wrongfully and without lawful authority, for the purpose of compelling another person to abstain from doing anything that he or she has a lawful right to do"

@ref s 423(1) (the punishments) (src:7522-7530)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 423(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 423(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7522-7530)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 423(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (4) In this section, military justice system participant has the same meaning as in subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act. The Act is not among the sources: the answer is taken as an input.
-- src:7541 | Definition of military justice system participant
-- src:7542 | (4) In this section, military justice system participant has the same meaning as in subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act.
@ref s 423.1(4) (src:7541-7542)
GIVEN `the person is a military justice system participant within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423.1(4) the person is a military justice system participant` MEANS
    `the person is a military justice system participant within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the same meaning as in subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act"

DECLARE `s 423.1 act of the accused` IS ONE OF
    `s 423.1(1) engage in conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear`

DECLARE `s 423.1(1) target` IS ONE OF
    `s 423.1(1) a group of persons or the general public, in order to impede the administration of criminal justice`   -- (a)
    `s 423.1(1) a justice system participant or military justice system participant, in order to impede them in the performance of their duties`   -- (b)
    `s 423.1(1) a journalist, in order to impede them in the transmission to the public of information in relation to a criminal organization`   -- (c)
    `s 423.1(1) a target that is none of those`

-- 423.1 (1) No person shall, without lawful authority, engage in any conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in (a) a group of persons or the general public in order to impede the administration of criminal justice; (b) a justice system participant or military justice system participant in order to impede him or her in the performance of his or her duties; or (c) a journalist in order to impede him or her in the transmission to the public of information in relation to a criminal organization.
-- src:7533 | Intimidation of a justice system participant or a journalist
-- src:7534 | 423.1 (1) No person shall, without lawful authority, engage in any conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in
-- src:7535 | (a) a group of persons or the general public in order to impede the administration of criminal justice;
-- src:7536 | (b) a justice system participant or military justice system participant in order to impede him or her in the performance of his or her duties; or
-- src:7537 | (c) a journalist in order to impede him or her in the transmission to the public of information in relation to a criminal organization.
@ref s 423.1(1) (src:7533-7537)
GIVEN `the person engages in conduct without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with the intent to provoke a state of fear` IS A BOOLEAN
      target IS A `s 423.1(1) target`
      `the target is a justice system participant, by s 2 justice system participant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the target is a military justice system participant, by s 423.1(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `ccc13 all of` (LIST JUST `the person engages in conduct without lawful authority`
                          , JUST `the person acts with the intent to provoke a state of fear`
                          , JUST (NOT (target EQUALS `s 423.1(1) a target that is none of those`))
                          , IF target EQUALS `s 423.1(1) a justice system participant or military justice system participant, in order to impede them in the performance of their duties`
                            THEN `ccc13 any of` (LIST `the target is a justice system participant, by s 2 justice system participant`, `the target is a military justice system participant, by s 423.1(4)`)
                            ELSE JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person shall, without lawful authority, engage in any conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in" the three targets named; a target outside them is outside the prohibition

@ref s 423.1(1) (the prohibition on the person) (src:7533-7537)
GIVEN `the prohibition covers the act, by s 423.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 423.1 act of the accused`
`s 423.1(1) the prohibition on the person` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition covers the act, by s 423.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the accused` SHANT `s 423.1(1) engage in conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:7538 | (2) [Repealed, 2015, c. 13, s. 12]
@ref s 423.1(2) (src:7538-7538)
`s 423.1(2) as the text shows it` MEANS "(2) [Repealed, 2015, c. 13, s. 12]"

