`s 423.1(3) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- the only limb the text states

@ref s 423.1(3) (the class of the offence) (src:7539-7540)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 423.1(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- (5) In this section, health professional means a person who is entitled under the laws of a province to provide health services.
-- src:7556 | Definition of health professional
-- src:7557 | (5) In this section, health professional means a person who is entitled under the laws of a province to provide health services.
@ref s 423.2(5) (src:7556-7557)
GIVEN `the person is entitled under the laws of a province to provide health services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423.2(5) the person is a health professional` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled under the laws of a province to provide health services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "health professional means a person who is entitled under the laws of a province to provide health services"

DECLARE `s 423.2(1) target` IS ONE OF
    `s 423.2(1) a person, in order to impede them from obtaining health services from a health professional`   -- (a)
    `s 423.2(1) a health professional, in order to impede them in the performance of their duties`   -- (b)
    `s 423.2(1) a person whose functions are to assist a health professional in the performance of the health professional’s duties, in order to impede that person in the performance of those functions`   -- (c)
    `s 423.2(1) a target that is none of those`

-- src:7543 | Intimidation — health services
-- src:7544 | 423.2 (1) Every person commits an offence who engages in any conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in
-- src:7545 | (a) a person in order to impede them from obtaining health services from a health professional;
-- src:7546 | (b) a health professional in order to impede them in the performance of their duties; or
-- src:7547 | (c) a person, whose functions are to assist a health professional in the performance of the health professional’s duties, in order to impede that person in the performance of those functions.
@ref s 423.2(1) (src:7543-7547)
GIVEN `the person engages in conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear` IS A BOOLEAN
      target IS A `s 423.2(1) target`
      `the health professional concerned is a health professional, by s 423.2(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423.2(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation of health services` MEANS
    IF `the person engages in conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear` AND NOT (target EQUALS `s 423.2(1) a target that is none of those`)
    THEN `the health professional concerned is a health professional, by s 423.2(5)`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who engages in any conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in"

-- (4) No person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2) by reason only that they attend at or near, or approach, a place referred to in that subsection for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information.
-- src:7554 | Defence
-- src:7555 | (4) No person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2) by reason only that they attend at or near, or approach, a place referred to in that subsection for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information.
@ref s 423.2(4) (src:7554-7555)
GIVEN `the person attends at or near, or approaches, a place referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423.2(4) the person is saved from guilt of an offence under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the person attends at or near, or approaches, a place referred to in subsection (2)` AND `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information"; this subsection gives no defence on these facts

-- src:7548 | Obstruction or interference with access
-- src:7549 | (2) Every person commits an offence who, without lawful authority, intentionally obstructs or interferes with another person’s lawful access to a place at which health services are provided by a health professional.
@ref s 423.2(2) (src:7548-7549)
GIVEN `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intentionally obstructs or interferes with another person’s lawful access to a place at which health services are provided by a health professional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the health professional concerned is a health professional, by s 423.2(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the defence applies, by s 423.2(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423.2(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to health services` MEANS
    IF `the person acts without lawful authority` AND `the person intentionally obstructs or interferes with another person’s lawful access to a place at which health services are provided by a health professional`
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the health professional concerned is a health professional, by s 423.2(5)`, `ccc13 not` `the defence applies, by s 423.2(4)`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who, without lawful authority, intentionally obstructs or interferes with another person’s lawful access"

