DECLARE `s 423.3(1) place` IS ONE OF
    `s 423.3(1) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used for religious worship`   -- (a)(i)
    `s 423.3(1) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group for administrative, social, cultural or sports activities or events`   -- (a)(ii)(A)
    `s 423.3(1) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group as an educational institution, including a daycare centre`   -- (a)(ii)(B)
    `s 423.3(1) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group as a residence for seniors`   -- (a)(ii)(C)
    `s 423.3(1) a cemetery`   -- (b)
    `s 423.3(1) a place that is none of those`

-- src:7558 | Intimidation — building used for religious worship, etc.
-- src:7559 | 423.3 (1) Every person commits an offence who engages in any conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in a person in order to impede their access to
-- src:7560 | (a) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used
-- src:7561 | (i) for religious worship, or
-- src:7562 | (ii) by an identifiable group, as defined in subsection 318(4),
-- src:7563 | (A) for administrative, social, cultural or sports activities or events,
-- src:7564 | (B) as an educational institution, including a daycare centre, or
-- src:7565 | (C) as a residence for seniors; or
-- src:7566 | (b) a cemetery.
@ref s 423.3(1) (src:7558-7566)
GIVEN `the person engages in conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in a person in order to impede their access to the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `s 423.3(1) place`
      `the group is an identifiable group, as defined in subsection 318(4), by s 318(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person engages in conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in a person in order to impede their access to the place`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who engages in any conduct with the intent to provoke a state of fear in a person in order to impede their access to"
    ELSE CONSIDER place
         WHEN `s 423.3(1) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used for religious worship` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 423.3(1) a cemetery` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 423.3(1) a place that is none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used"
         OTHERWISE `the group is an identifiable group, as defined in subsection 318(4), by s 318(4)`   -- (a)(ii): JUST TRUE for an identifiable group; the answer of s 318(4) otherwise

-- (4) No person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2) by reason only that they attend at or near, or approach, a building or structure referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or a cemetery for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information.
-- src:7573 | Exception
-- src:7574 | (4) No person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2) by reason only that they attend at or near, or approach, a building or structure referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or a cemetery for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information.
@ref s 423.3(4) (src:7573-7574)
GIVEN `the person attends at or near, or approaches, a building or structure referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or a cemetery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423.3(4) the person is saved from guilt of an offence under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the person attends at or near, or approaches, a building or structure referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or a cemetery` AND `the person does so for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information"; this subsection gives no exception on these facts

-- src:7567 | Obstruction or interference with access
-- src:7568 | (2) Every person commits an offence who, without lawful authority, intentionally obstructs or interferes with another person’s lawful access to a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or to a cemetery.
@ref s 423.3(2) (src:7567-7568)
GIVEN `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intentionally obstructs or interferes with another person’s lawful access to the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is one referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or a cemetery, by s 423.3(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the exception applies, by s 423.3(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 423.3(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` MEANS
    IF `the person acts without lawful authority` AND `the person intentionally obstructs or interferes with another person’s lawful access to the place`
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the place is one referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or a cemetery, by s 423.3(1)`, `ccc13 not` `the exception applies, by s 423.3(4)`)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who, without lawful authority, intentionally obstructs or interferes with another person’s lawful access"

