`s 424.1 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 424.1 (the class of the offence) (src:7579-7582)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 424.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- 425 Every one who, being an employer or the agent of an employer, wrongfully and without lawful authority (a) refuses to employ or dismisses from his employment any person for the reason only that the person is a member of a lawful trade union ...,
-- (b) seeks by intimidation, threat of loss of position or employment, ... to compel workmen or employees to abstain from belonging to any trade union ..., or (c) conspires, combines, agrees or arranges with any other employer or his agent to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b), is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:7583 | Offences by employers
-- src:7584 | 425 Every one who, being an employer or the agent of an employer, wrongfully and without lawful authority
-- src:7585 | (a) refuses to employ or dismisses from his employment any person for the reason only that the person is a member of a lawful trade union or of a lawful association or combination of workmen or employees formed for the purpose of advancing, in a lawful manner, their interests and organized for their protection in the regulation of wages and conditions of work,
-- src:7586 | (b) seeks by intimidation, threat of loss of position or employment, or by causing actual loss of position or employment, or by threatening or imposing any pecuniary penalty, to compel workmen or employees to abstain from belonging to any trade union, association or combination to which they have a lawful right to belong, or
-- src:7587 | (c) conspires, combines, agrees or arranges with any other employer or his agent to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b),
-- src:7588 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 425 (src:7583-7588)
GIVEN `the person is an employer or the agent of an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts wrongfully and without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person refuses to employ or dismisses from their employment any person for the reason only that the person is a member of a lawful trade union or of a lawful association or combination of workmen or employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person seeks by intimidation, threat of loss of position or employment, or by causing actual loss of position or employment, or by threatening or imposing any pecuniary penalty, to compel workmen or employees to abstain from belonging to any trade union, association or combination to which they have a lawful right to belong` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person conspires, combines, agrees or arranges with any other employer or their agent to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 425 the conduct is the offence of an employer discriminating against trade unionists` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an employer or the agent of an employer`
      AND `the person acts wrongfully and without lawful authority`
      AND (   `the person refuses to employ or dismisses from their employment any person for the reason only that the person is a member of a lawful trade union or of a lawful association or combination of workmen or employees`   -- (a)
           OR `the person seeks by intimidation, threat of loss of position or employment, or by causing actual loss of position or employment, or by threatening or imposing any pecuniary penalty, to compel workmen or employees to abstain from belonging to any trade union, association or combination to which they have a lawful right to belong`   -- (b)
           OR `the person conspires, combines, agrees or arranges with any other employer or their agent to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)`)   -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who, being an employer or the agent of an employer, wrongfully and without lawful authority"

@ref s 425 (the punishments) (src:7583-7588)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 425 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 1: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 425 (the class of the offence) (src:7583-7588)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 425 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- 425.1 (1) No employer or person acting on behalf of an employer or in a position of authority in respect of an employee of the employer shall take a disciplinary measure against, demote, terminate or otherwise adversely affect the employment of such an employee, or threaten to do so,
-- (a) with the intent to compel the employee to abstain from providing information to a person whose duties include the enforcement of federal or provincial law, respecting an offence ...; or (b) with the intent to retaliate against the employee because the employee has provided information referred to in paragraph (a) ...
-- src:7589 | Threats and retaliation against employees
-- src:7590 | 425.1 (1) No employer or person acting on behalf of an employer or in a position of authority in respect of an employee of the employer shall take a disciplinary measure against, demote, terminate or otherwise adversely affect the employment of such an employee, or threaten to do so,
-- src:7591 | (a) with the intent to compel the employee to abstain from providing information to a person whose duties include the enforcement of federal or provincial law, respecting an offence that the employee believes has been or is being committed contrary to this or any other federal or provincial Act or regulation by the employer or an officer or employee of the employer or, if the employer is a corporation, by one or more of its directors; or
-- src:7592 | (b) with the intent to retaliate against the employee because the employee has provided information referred to in paragraph (a) to a person whose duties include the enforcement of federal or provincial law.
@ref s 425.1(1) (src:7589-7592)
GIVEN `the person is an employer or a person acting on behalf of an employer or in a position of authority in respect of an employee of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person takes a disciplinary measure against, demotes, terminates or otherwise adversely affects the employment of such an employee, or threatens to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to compel the employee to abstain from providing information to a person whose duties include the enforcement of federal or provincial law, respecting an offence that the employee believes has been or is being committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intent is to retaliate against the employee because the employee has provided such information to a person whose duties include the enforcement of federal or provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 425.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an employer or a person acting on behalf of an employer or in a position of authority in respect of an employee of the employer`
      AND `the person takes a disciplinary measure against, demotes, terminates or otherwise adversely affects the employment of such an employee, or threatens to do so`
      AND (`the intent is to compel the employee to abstain from providing information to a person whose duties include the enforcement of federal or provincial law, respecting an offence that the employee believes has been or is being committed` OR `the intent is to retaliate against the employee because the employee has provided such information to a person whose duties include the enforcement of federal or provincial law`)   -- (a), (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No employer or person acting on behalf of an employer or in a position of authority in respect of an employee of the employer shall"; a person or act outside that description is outside the prohibition

DECLARE `s 425.1 act of the accused` IS ONE OF
    `s 425.1(1) take a disciplinary measure against, demote, terminate or otherwise adversely affect the employment of an employee, or threaten to do so`

@ref s 425.1(1) (the prohibition on the person) (src:7589-7592)
GIVEN `the prohibition covers the act, by s 425.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 425.1 act of the accused`
`s 425.1(1) the prohibition on the person` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition covers the act, by s 425.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the accused` SHANT `s 425.1(1) take a disciplinary measure against, demote, terminate or otherwise adversely affect the employment of an employee, or threaten to do so`
    ELSE FULFILLED

