    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "principal includes an employer"; the list is not closed

-- 426 (1) Every one commits an offence who (a) directly or indirectly, corruptly gives, offers or agrees to give or offer to an agent or to anyone for the benefit of the agent -- or, being an agent, directly or indirectly, corruptly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept from any person, for themselves or another person --
-- any reward, advantage or benefit of any kind as consideration for doing or not doing, or for having done or not done, any act relating to the affairs or business of the agent's principal, or for showing or not showing favour or disfavour ...; or (b) with intent to deceive a principal, gives to an agent of that principal, or, being an agent, uses with intent to deceive his principal, a receipt, an account or other writing (i) ... (ii) ... and (iii) ...
-- src:7598 | Secret Commissions
-- src:7599 | Secret commissions
-- src:7600 | 426 (1) Every one commits an offence who
-- src:7601 | (a) directly or indirectly, corruptly gives, offers or agrees to give or offer to an agent or to anyone for the benefit of the agent — or, being an agent, directly or indirectly, corruptly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept from any person, for themselves or another person — any reward, advantage or benefit of any kind as consideration for doing or not doing, or for having done or not done, any act relating to the affairs or business of the agent’s principal, or for showing or not showing favour or disfavour to any person with relation to the affairs or business of the agent’s principal; or
-- src:7602 | (b) with intent to deceive a principal, gives to an agent of that principal, or, being an agent, uses with intent to deceive his principal, a receipt, an account or other writing
-- src:7603 | (i) in which the principal has an interest,
-- src:7604 | (ii) that contains any statement that is false or erroneous or defective in any material particular, and
-- src:7605 | (iii) that is intended to mislead the principal.
@ref s 426(1) (src:7598-7605)
GIVEN `the person corruptly gives, offers or agrees to give or offer to an agent or to anyone for the benefit of the agent, or, being an agent, corruptly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept from any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reward, advantage or benefit of any kind is consideration for doing or not doing, or for having done or not done, any act relating to the affairs or business of the agent’s principal, or for showing or not showing favour or disfavour to any person with relation to the affairs or business of the agent’s principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, with intent to deceive a principal, gives to an agent of that principal, or, being an agent, uses with intent to deceive their principal, a receipt, an account or other writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is one in which the principal has an interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing contains a statement that is false or erroneous or defective in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is intended to mislead the principal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is an agent, by s 426(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 426(1) the conduct is the offence of a secret commission` MEANS
    IF    (    `the person corruptly gives, offers or agrees to give or offer to an agent or to anyone for the benefit of the agent, or, being an agent, corruptly demands, accepts or offers or agrees to accept from any person`   -- (a)
           AND `the reward, advantage or benefit of any kind is consideration for doing or not doing, or for having done or not done, any act relating to the affairs or business of the agent’s principal, or for showing or not showing favour or disfavour to any person with relation to the affairs or business of the agent’s principal`)
       OR (    `the person, with intent to deceive a principal, gives to an agent of that principal, or, being an agent, uses with intent to deceive their principal, a receipt, an account or other writing`   -- (b)
           AND `the writing is one in which the principal has an interest`
           AND `the writing contains a statement that is false or erroneous or defective in a material particular`
           AND `the writing is intended to mislead the principal`)
    THEN `the other person is an agent, by s 426(4)`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who"

-- src:7606 | Privity to offence
-- src:7607 | (2) Every one commits an offence who is knowingly privy to the commission of an offence under subsection (1).
